      "content": "The model cut off again right in the middle of the Weibull formula. Can you finish that? \n\nAlso, I'm trying to understand—you mentioned \"fitting a distribution\" to the data. When the data is this messy and unpredictable, how do I know if I've actually captured all the \"weirdness\" in the pattern? Is there a specific statistical way to measure if the distribution I've chosen is actually accounting for those massive, random spikes in lead time, or am I just guessing?",
